  <!--
    EvictingQueue<T> is a Kotlin class implementing java.util.Queue<T>. Kotlin satisfies the
    interface through inherited/delegated members that class-parse does not see as declared on the
    type, so the generator emits a class that claims to implement ICollection without emitting
    ContainsAll, RemoveAll, RetainAll or Size - four CS0535 errors, and not something a binding
    definition can fix by adding members, because the JNI signatures it would need belong to the
    delegate.

    It is removed rather than hand-completed: it lives in com.datadog.android.internal.collections,
    is a bounded FIFO used inside the SDK's own buffering, and appears in no other bound member's
    signature - verified against api.xml, where the only references are its own declaration. If a
    future release exposes it on a public API, this rule will start failing that member instead of
    silently hiding it.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.datadog.android.internal.collections']/class[@name='EvictingQueue']" />

